DESCRIPTION:Discussion for parents\, educators and community members who a
 re concerned about digital and online product use in classrooms.\nSource: 
 Brooks Memorial Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6384703dca2b948b@kidcal
DTSTAMP:20261113T182525Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261116T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261116T193000
SUMMARY:Ahead of the Curb: Minimizing Household Waste to Maximize Communit
 y Composting
LOCATION:Main Reading Room
URL:https://brookslibraryvt.org/event/ahead-of-the-curb-minimizing-househo
 ld-waste-to-maximize-community-composting-2/
CATEGORIES:kids\,Brooks Memorial Library
DESCRIPTION:Join Alex Lacy\, outreach coordinator for WSWMD\, and Stephen 
 Dotson\, sustainability coordinator for the town of Brattleboro\, on Monda
 y\, November 9th from 4:30-6 pm – and on Monday November 16th from 6-7:3
 0 pm:\n\n\nGather round to receive updates and important information about
  the Brattleboro curbside compost program. Alex Lacy\, outreach coordinato
 r at WSWMD\, and Stephen Dotson\, sustainability coordinator with the town
  of Brattleboro\, will be present to run down the basics of the service\, 
 explain what changes have been made and why\, and to demonstrate how the t
 own’s cooperation is helping our local economy as well as support farmer
 s and gardeners alike. Municipal composting is a welcome service in a town
  where not everyone is composting in their backyard\, not to mention in a 
 state that has mandated a ban on food scraps in the landfill. Composting n
 ot only avoids pollution of methane into our atmosphere\, it results in a 
 healthy additive to the soil when used as intended. Appropriate use of qua
 lity compost has the potential to increase garden yields and help plants t
 o fight off disease. Quality compost comes from quality inputs into the co
 mpost. This is a chance to bring your questions and concerns over what is 
 and what is not acceptable in your curbside bin to an open discussion foll
 owing a brief presentation.\nSource: Brooks Memorial Library
END:VEVENT
